te's F3 was the move that sealed the center."}, {"turn": 29, "text": "F1 was the costliest move of the game, losing 29.6 points and taking the lead from -51.9 to -81.5. The engine's choice was B4, a move on the left that Black only played later, at 33, after the damage was done. The 20k's reply E1 also lost 25.2 points, but the game was already far out of reach."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Everything it ran was inspection or bookkeeping: `inspectLiberties` from current-position-liberties.js listed chains and liberties on the current board, `check` applied one player-named move to report captures and the resulting chain, and the remaining commands called the play tool, replayed actual moves, built the SGF and wrote game notes. None of it looped over empty points to rank candidates or played a sequence forward.", "stop": false}}